# Empire backup lessons (locked)

Every correction below was a hole in an Empire import, or a behavior locked after that import. The next backup, for this company or any other, must come in already corrected. Do not wipe a live company to retest. Apply the repair to the books that are already there, and keep the same repair on the import path.

Keep noting. Whenever a change is made to how a backup is read, how a voucher posts, how a ledger or outstanding is calculated, or how an entry or report behaves, add the next number in this file in the same sitting as the code change. Name the series and the column when the change came from the backup. Do not leave the change only in the chat.

1. **Work despatch pending.** The receipt's CHALLAN column is the job worker's bill number. The despatch it consumed is on each BILLDET line: ORDBILL (challan no), ORDTYPE (series code), orderno (despatch voucher). Link that line only to that despatch. Do not guess by quality, and do not spill a line onto the next challan. A line with no pick consumes nothing. On a new bill whose other lines already name their challans, an extra line with no challan (a sample received without a despatch) is saved and must not block the entry. The export must include those three columns. Check: Bhagwati voucher 20 (bill 57) is 120 pcs from challan 6 and 120 from challan 7. Pending before invoice 59 is **712 pcs on challans 5, 6 and 7** (112, 240 and 360). Repair: `repairWorkDespatchLinks`.

2. **State is the GSTIN, not the city.** Empire STATE1 is often the city (SURAT, JAUNPUR). GST state is the first two digits of the GSTIN. A place that is not a real state must not be treated as interstate. City stays in the city field. Repair: `repairPartyStatesFromGstin`.

3. **Sale amount.** Post the full invoice (BILLAMT). `finalamt` is after the bill discount. Do not store `finalamt − taxable` in `shippingCharge` and then post that as the sale. The imported discount is the V1 journal, posted once. A bank-receipt discount is credited only when no same-day V1 of that amount already hits the party, on the debit or the credit (within ₹1). Laxmi receipt 118 on 7/5/2026 has a ₹9 discount on bill 2025/F, and V1 voucher 10 the same day is Dr party 9. The receipt must not credit that ₹9 again. The party balance is 260142.

4. **Opening balance** (series 00) is the brought-forward figure. Vouchers before 1 April are already inside it. Do not add them again. A March bill's April discount journal stays; the March sale does not.

5. **Outstanding** hides opening journals, bill-tagged VATAV, settled returns, and unadjusted balances that a later receipt already used. O57 sales challans are not invoices.

6. **Bank and cash.** Voucher numbers are per series. Bills, discounts, and unadjusted picks on a receipt must be imported onto that voucher. Do not auto-pick unadjusted payments. Disc % fills Disc Amt from the bill amount. The default bank is the most-used account.

7. **Journals.** The opposite account list must include the imported P&L, trading, and asset heads. A journal whose party is a debtor posts on the customer when the supplier is missing. A new journal party asks to add the account.

8. **Work-bill discount and line amount.** DISCOUNT and billdis can be 0 while VAT was charged on a lower base. Bhagwati job bills are 12% off; recover that percent from gross and tax (`impliedDiscountPercent`) and do not also invent a second discount journal. Keep the imported line amount when it is not pieces × rate (P7 19, 120 pcs, rate 255, Empire amount 30090).

9. **Company-named series** stay out of general pick lists. COMPULSORY LINK stays optional. The pending quantity still has to fall when a receipt was adjusted against a challan.

10. **Cheque return.** FAS remark `CHEQUE RETN. ON` on a bank receipt (B1) means that receipt no longer pays its bills. The bounce is a separate bank payment (B2) dated the return date, remark `CHQ RETURN`. Re-presenting the cheque adds a new bank receipt with the same bills. The remark is already on the imported row, so the books that are already there release those bills without another import. Neither voucher is an unadjusted balance. Laxmi receipt 415 of 53260 on 17/09/2026 stays off outstanding.

11. **Work despatch category.** BILLDET.CATEGORY is the design on each despatch line (challan 232/L is FRANDY FABRIC three times: DARK BHAYA 240, BHAVYA DUSTY 300, BHAVYA COCO 180). A receipt line links to the despatch line of the same quality and category (O11 / P31). Linking only by quality leaves the other designs pending. The pick list shows one row per line. Repair: `repairWorkDespatchLinks` stamps CATEGORY from billdet, then allocates. Check: 232/L stays fully pending, and 225/L COCO BHAVYA pending is 149.

12. **Bill round-off.** Sale bills, purchase bills, and debit/credit notes post to the nearest rupee, including the Empire bills. The paise on those invoices (0.28, 0.16, 0.40) are the round-off. A receipt that is under ₹1 away from the bill settles it, so that paise does not stay outstanding and the party ledger is in rupees. Journals stay in paise. TDS posts to the next rupee (541.01 becomes 542) on mill, work receipt, and commission. Repair: `repairBillRoundOff`.

13. **Note picked on a receipt.** RECPAY can settle a debit or credit note on the same voucher as the bills. That amount is applied, so it must not come back as an unadjusted balance. Laxmi receipt 56 on 21/04/2026 pays debit note 13/D of 4057 with bills 1791/F, 1792/F and 1796/F. The note's own pending is the bank allocation; once that allocation exists the note is off outstanding.

14. **VATAV with one FAS line.** Series V1 usually has two lines: DISCOUNT A/C and the party. Nine vouchers (137, 138, 139, 140, 164, 165, 166, 168, 169) have only the party credit in FAS `code`, with the bill number in RMK. The missing side is DISCOUNT A/C, the account on every other V1. An empty opposite account must not become SUSPENSE for V1. The party credit stays. Repair: set that opposite account to DISCOUNT A/C. Suspense on these books was 4,766 DR from those nine.

15. **Less fold.** BILLDET.LESSFOLD is the fold on that line, on sale and purchase. It is copied as entered. The sale bill prints it as what remains of 100. A later import must not leave the column blank.

16. **Piece or metre.** BILLDET.AMT decides the unit. If the amount matches metres × rate, the line is MTS. If it matches pieces × rate, it stays PCS. The Empire voucher number is kept when that bill is opened again.

17. **Printed bill number.** Finish sales uses the number on the bill (BILLS.BILL), the digits before any star or letter. A voucher stored at 100000 or above is the same printed number. The series suffix stays on the series, not glued into the number the user types.

18. **Grey taka and mill receipt.** CHALTRN metres (WMTS, MMTS, RMTS, CMTS) are the taka rows of that mill dispatch, joined by CARDNO. Each MILLREC row keeps its voucher, mill, job rate, received pieces and metres, and the despatch it came from (CARDNO or DESPNO). TDS on that bill rounds up to the next rupee.

19. **Account heads and brokers.** Every MASTER row is an account under its ATYPE name: debtors, creditors, expenses, trading, and assets. A head used on a voucher but missing from MASTER is still created. MASTER.commission is the broker percent. A broker stays a creditor. PINVTRN.BROKER_CODE is the broker on the mill dispatch. Expense heads such as Travelling must appear on a purchase bill and on the journal opposite list.

These live in the software. A later backup does not replace them, and they are not rebuilt unless the user says that one is still wrong.

20. **Keyboard entry.** Enter moves to the next field. Enter at the end of a filled line adds the next line and focuses its first field. Two Enters on that blank line ask to save. Down, then Enter, on a blank line also asks to save. F9 saves. The mouse Add Line button stays.

21. **Sale bill print.** The bill prints as one full A4 tax invoice from its own page. The ERP screen is not what is sent to the printer.

22. **Open the voucher from the row.** A ledger or report row opens that voucher in edit. Back returns one step and keeps the party search.

23. **GST on entry.** A party with no GSTIN is asked before the entry continues. GST type can be Local, Interstate, or Non GST. Non GST sets the rate to 0. If the master has no GST and the user continues, the type follows the GSTIN.

24. **LR, rate, and photo.** LR number and LR date can be entered on one sale bill or on many bills together. The rate and cut last typed for an item are remembered on the next bill. A photo fill follows the sales type already selected. E-way and e-invoice stay as built. Poonam and Sunita e-way mode are left as they are unless the user asks to change them.

25. **Less fold percent and finish-purchase voucher.** Printed FOLD is out of 100. FOLD 95 is less fold 5 (`100 − fold`). Net metres = gross MTS × (100 − less fold) / 100. A metre line (MTR) is billed at that net × rate. The entry grid shows Net Mtrs beside MTS on finish purchase and finish sale. A photo stores the PCS column as pieces, the MTS column as gross metres, and the printed fold as less fold. Finish purchase (P2) next voucher ignores `typeBillNumber` ≥ 100000, which are prior-year copies. Aishwarya Fashion supplier bill 630 dated 18/11/2026 is finish purchase voucher 226.

26. **Work-bill payment.** A bank payment pending list includes work receipt bills, not only purchase bills. The Type pick is the series: WORK REC. LACE BILLS (P31) shows that series. A challan series is not a bill. Pending is the invoice minus that bill's TDS (TDS to the next rupee), minus a bank payment already adjusted on that receipt (`billType` work_receipt). Virendra Kumar Ashok Prasad Verma's lace bills 1–12 are settled. Bill 13 (46,752) and voucher 274 (15,589) stay pending.

27. **Sales order fold and bundle cut.** A sales order line has Less Fold and Net Mtrs, the same columns as a finish sale. Net metres = gross MTS × (100 − less fold) / 100, and a metre line is priced on that net. Bundles accepts `30*24`: 30 pieces, cut 24, 720 metres. A list with no star, such as `24.5+22+23.5`, is 3 pieces, cut 0, and metres are the sum. The typed text stays in Bundles. A later backup must keep less fold on the order line.

28. **HSN from the item master.** Quality Information HSN is the bill HSN. Korean Silk stored as 540752 must not stay on the series default 5407. Picking the item fills the line and the bill HSN from `hsnSac`.

29. **Sales order lines on a sale bill.** Picking a sales order copies each of its lines. Order 7 stays 20×24 (480 m, cut 24) and the 10-piece list (216 m, cut 0). It must not become one Korean Silk line of 30 pcs with cut 23. Cut is not rewritten as metres ÷ pieces. The bundle text of each line is kept.

30. **Sales A/C.** FINISH SALES and FINISH SALES (GST) credit SALES A/C with the invoice (the same figure the party is debited) and debit the GST on that bill. The imported VAT JV is the same GST and must not be posted again. A bill with no VAT JV, such as 1468/F through 1478/F, still shows its GST. Empire's GST debit on this account to 18/11/2026 is 23,40,829.53. The sale credit is the invoice, not only the GST.

31. **Bill discount is not outstanding.** The discount stays on the sale bill. FINISH SALES (GST) keeps BILLAMT as the invoice, and the line discount stays on the bill. `finalamt` is after the bill discount; an imported bill stores `finalamt − taxable` in `shippingCharge`. When that is below the GST, outstanding pending drops that gap. The receipt still shows the sale bill at the invoice minus the money received. Shivpriya Silk Mills 23/F stays invoice 52,039 with discount 1,489; outstanding pending is 0. A bank receipt for a name that is also a supplier still lists that party's sale bills. A bank payment still lists the purchase bills.
